{% section id="log" title="Decisions / Deviations Log" %}
- 2026-07-29: Initial plan created from investigation of the Heddle panel registry, DesignSystemPage, panel-manifest, panel-builder templates, panel-authoring examples, and the Weft/Heddle repo boundary. Six panels in scope; P5/P6 gated on version decisions by Katie (Content Explorer) and Aaron + Katie (Updated Dashboard).
- 2026-07-29: Added the Panel visual survey section — live captures of all six panels from the develop demo routes, plus the competing Working Threads variant (codex_updates_dashboard_verification) and the PR 496 theme-following board, so version reconciliation can happen in this doc.
- 2026-07-29: Research correction for P5: PR 242 (katie/nod-978) was closed and superseded by merged PR 244 — develop's Content Overview is the evolved nod-978 work. P5's checkpoint becomes a confirmation, not a version pick.
- 2026-07-29: Spun up the companion decision doc "WIP Panel Version Comparison — Content Explorer & Updated Dashboard" (`https://doct.nodaste.com/d/workspace_6dbf05f0-fc4b-41f4-b927-5799ec7be0bb/docs/04403f7e-6668-4183-ad51-034548c3faab`) with per-region commentable panel anatomy, because screenshot-only surveys can't take in-panel comments. P5/P6 checkpoints now route through it.
- 2026-07-29: Research correction for P6: PR 270 (katie/nod-1051) merged as Settings → Spaces, a different surface. Live dashboard candidates: develop's merged Updates Dashboard board vs PR 496 (theme-following board, NOD-1254), with codex_updates_dashboard_verification iterating on Working Threads identity attribution.
{% /section %}

{% section id="resume" title="Resume Instructions (Agent)" %}
Read this plan fully, then inspect the first unchecked Progress item. P1–P4 may be worked in any order; do not start P5 or P6 past their checkpoint steps unless the corresponding version decision is recorded in the Decisions / Deviations Log. Follow the Heddle-vs-Weft boundary in `weft/AGENTS.md` for every file placement, keep examples token-clean per the shared raw-color pattern, and update the matching Progress checkbox plus a dated log line after each phase.
{% /section %}
